on-arrival: {!
let severity =
    4 +
    (Number(Q.anti_ukrainian_pressure) || 0) * 0.10 +
    (Number(Q.border_permission_pressure) || 0) * 0.08 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        12 - (Number(Q.refugee_service_capacity) || 0)
    ) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, 45 - (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 0)) * 0.10;
if (Q.refugee_settlement == "End alleged Ukrainian preferences") {
    severity += 4;
}
if (Q.asylum_position_2025 == "Supported temporary asylum suspension") {
    severity += 3;
}
if (
    Q.refugee_settlement == "Funded receiving-community services" ||
    Q.refugee_settlement == "Equal and transparent benefit rules"
) {
    severity -= 3;
}
Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 = Math.max(
    3,
    Math.min(20, Math.round(severity))
);
Q.anti_ukrainian_pressure += Q.hate_incident_severity_2026;
Q.minority_safety -= Math.max(
    2,
    Math.round(Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 * 0.55)
);
Q.refugee_empathy -= Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 * 0.30)
);
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -8;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 9;
Q.news_headline =
    "Anti-Ukrainian hostility crosses from rhetoric into reported incidents";
!}

= October 2026 — More reports do not reveal the whole trend

**Myroslava Keryk**, head of the Ukrainian House foundation, says families are
changing routes to work and deciding which insults are worth reporting. Police
register more anti-Ukrainian incidents, but the increase cannot answer its own
meaning. It may reflect more violence, more trust in reporting, or both; poor
classification can hide either trend.

[? if refugee_service_capacity >= 12 and minority_safety >= 45: Earlier
investment in local services and equal rules has left victims with offices and
people they recognise. The new reports are alarming partly because silence is
no longer the only safe response.?][? if border_permission_pressure >= 45 or
minority_safety < 45: Repeated concessions to collective suspicion have made
anti-Ukrainian rhetoric sound administrative before it becomes violent. Many
victims still expect reporting to create a second danger.?][? if
refugee_service_capacity < 12 and border_permission_pressure < 45 and
minority_safety >= 45: Lewica's earlier record is mixed: it rejected collective
blame without building enough durable local help. Police have a category, but
not yet a trusted route into it.?]

Keryk asks for victim support; police want a usable classification; prosecutors
want files they can prove; border towns want security arguments that do not
license private vengeance. Lewica must decide which institution brings those
demands together.

- @hate_reporting
- @hate_prosecution
- @hate_opposition_bill
- @hate_joint_doctrine
- @hate_denial

@hate_reporting
title: Fund victim reporting, legal aid and transparent classifications
subtitle: Put Ukrainian House and local legal-aid desks between frightened witnesses and an unfamiliar police form. Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The support network cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; border_response_2026 = "Victim reporting and transparent classification"; minority_safety += 6; police_trust += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; anti_ukrainian_pressure -= 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A reporting network makes violence more visible and more prosecutable"

Ukrainian House, municipal lawyers and trained interpreters open one reporting
route, while police publish how incidents are classified and corrected. The
number may rise again as hidden cases enter the record. Victims gain an advocate
and prosecutors gain usable files; Lewica promises not to call visibility a
policy failure merely because it makes the first chart worse.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the reporting route

@hate_prosecution
title: Create specialist prosecutor and police teams
subtitle: Bring a cabinet motion for specialist teams and fund it; the serving interior and justice ministers retain command. Cost: 1 budget capacity.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Lewica must hold cabinet authority and fund specialist capacity.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
Q.minority_safety += 5;
Q.border_response_2026 =
    "Specialist hate-crime police and prosecutor teams";
Q.prosecution_command_clarity += 3;
Q.police_trust += 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 6;
Q.news_headline = "Specialist teams turn reports into cases";
!}

The cabinet authorises paired police and prosecutor teams with published
charging guidance. Lewica has won the decision, not personal command over
investigators: the serving interior and justice ministers remain accountable
for appointments and cases. Reports now have somewhere specialised to go, and
every failure will carry a ministry's name.

- @poland_event_queue: Take it to cabinet

@hate_opposition_bill
title: Table a specialist-team bill and publish vacancy data
subtitle: From opposition, expose the empty posts and give the cabinet a funded structure it can adopt or reject. Cost: 1 resource.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary oversight team cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; border_response_2026 = "Opposition specialist-team bill and vacancy audit"; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 3; media_capacity += 3; minority_safety += 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Lewica demands specialist teams without pretending to command police or prosecutors"

Lewica tables a bill with posts, training and reporting duties, then publishes
the vacancies that prevent existing units from acting. No officer or prosecutor
is appointed by an opposition club. The government must nevertheless choose in
public between funding the structure and explaining why the files can wait.

- @poland_event_queue: Table the bill

@hate_joint_doctrine
title: Convene officers, border towns, unions and rights groups around one doctrine
subtitle: Ask Keryk, officers, mayors, unions and rights lawyers to write one rule for safety without collective blame. Cost: 2 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 2 and border_security_confidence >= 48 and border_rights_standard >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: Earlier choices left one side of the security-and-rights coalition without enough trust.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; border_response_2026 = "Joint secure-and-lawful border convention"; border_doctrine = "Joint secure-and-lawful operating doctrine"; border_security_confidence += 4; border_rights_standard += 5; minority_safety += 7; refugee_empathy += 4; police_trust += 3; military_trust += 2; anti_ukrainian_pressure -= 6; far_right_agenda -= 3; local_network += 2; public_trust += 4; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 7; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 6; news_headline = "A joint border convention breaks the security-versus-humanity script"

The convention separates hostile acts from nationality, border enforcement
from street vengeance, and police discretion from silence. Keryk's advocates
gain referral rules; officers gain a standard they can defend in tense towns;
unions and mayors gain a way to discuss wages and services without making
Ukrainian residents the explanation for every shortage. Nobody gets every
slogan, which is why the doctrine can be used.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the parties

@hate_denial
title: Reject the trend as media exaggeration
subtitle: Treat imperfect data as proof that no political response is owed.
on-arrival: border_response_2026 = "Denial of the reported trend"; anti_ukrainian_pressure += 8; minority_safety -= 7; police_trust -= 2; far_right_agenda += 5; public_trust -= 3; border_permission_pressure += 6; news_headline = "Denial tells victims that reporting is another political risk"

Lewica attacks the statistics and leaves the testimonies inside them
unanswered. Keryk's staff tell victims that a report may now make them part of
a partisan dispute; officers lose any incentive to improve classifications the
party will dismiss. The far right learns that it can move the argument from
whether hostility is justified to whether its targets should be believed.

- @poland_event_queue: Dispute the figures

@rozwoj_internal_pis_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — The variable name and the note to the auditor are gone; the blocked branch now says why an internal current is the worse outcome for Lewica — Kaczyński keeps every mandate and gains a modernising face. It remains a short bulletin with no decision attached.
title: Rozwój+ remains a PiS internal current
subtitle: The premiership, Szydło's leadership or a PiS–Lewica coalition closes the route to a separate party
face-image: img/poland/events/mateusz-morawiecki-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 28
order: 12
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ((year = 2026 and month = 10) or (year = 2026 and month = 5 and rozwoj_early_route)) and rozwoj_chain_stage = 4 and rozwoj_split_blocked
on-arrival: {!
Q.rozwoj_internal_pis = 1;
Q.rozwoj_club_formed = 0;
Q.rozwoj_party_formed = 0;
Q.pis_split = 0;
Q.pis_split_crisis = 0;
Q.rozwoj_chain_stage = 5;
const association = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "rozwoj_plus";
});
if (association) {
    association.active = 1;
    association.kind = "current";
    association.bloc = "pis";
    association.parent = "Prawo i Sprawiedliwość";
    association.allied = 1;
    association.legal_status = "internal PiS sub-party/current";
    association.exclusive_seats = 0;
}
Q.rozwoj_party_result =
    "Rozwój+ remains an internal PiS sub-party/current; no external split";
Q.news_headline = Q.rozwoj_party_result;
!}

= [+ rozwoj_party_result +]

Rozwój+ keeps its name, organisers and developmental programme, but it does not
become a separate parliamentary party. With **[+ prime_minister +]** leading,
or with PiS and Lewica sharing a cabinet, an external Morawiecki bloc would
either fracture the governing mandate or make the coalition unworkable.

The named deputies keep their PiS seats and their PiS whip. What Morawiecki has
built is a faction with letterhead — offices, a programme, a conference — inside
a party that has not lost a single mandate to it.

For us that is the worse outcome. A separate Rozwój+ would have split the right
and been answerable for its own record. An internal current gives Kaczyński a
modernising face to show voters who dislike him, while the seats stay exactly
where they were.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the internal current

@pis_party_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Morawiecki, Kaczyński, the named parliamentary network and Matysiak now carry each registration outcome, an association, club and party remain distinct, and all four Lewica responses receive branch-specific political aftermaths.
title: Rozwój+ decides whether to register a party
subtitle: Morawiecki has tested Kaczyński's discipline; now he must prove that a parliamentary rebellion can live outside the Sejm
face-image: img/poland/events/mateusz-morawiecki-2023.webp
