view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ((year = 2026 and month = 10) or (year = 2026 and month = 5 and rozwoj_early_route)) and rozwoj_chain_stage = 4 and not rozwoj_split_blocked
on-arrival: {!
const association = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "rozwoj_plus";
});
const organisation = association ? Number(association.organisation) || 0 : 0;
const cohesion = association ? Number(association.cohesion) || 0 : 0;
const developmentalMood = Math.max(
    -8,
    Math.min(
        12,
        ((Number(Q.economic_issue_salience) || 40) -
            (Number(Q.cultural_issue_salience) || 30)) * 0.18 +
        ((Number(Q.social_spending_support) || 50) - 50) * 0.10 +
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.08
    )
);
Q.rozwoj_social_mood_score = Math.round(developmentalMood);
Q.rozwoj_party_readiness += Math.round(developmentalMood);
Q.rozwoj_party_formed =
    Q.rozwoj_club_formed &&
    organisation >= 48 && cohesion >= 55 &&
    Q.rozwoj_party_readiness >= 28 ? 1 : 0;
Q.rozwoj_party_result = Q.rozwoj_party_formed
    ? "Rozwój+ registers as a political party"
    : (Q.rozwoj_club_formed
        ? "The club postpones party registration"
        : "The association remains outside party politics");
Q.rozwoj_chain_stage = 5;
if (association) {
    association.kind = Q.rozwoj_party_formed ? "party" : "association";
    association.bloc = Q.rozwoj_party_formed ? "rozwoj" : "pis";
    association.parent = Q.rozwoj_party_formed ? "Rozwój+" : association.parent;
    association.allied = Q.rozwoj_party_formed ? 0 : association.allied;
    association.legal_status = Q.rozwoj_party_formed
        ? "registered party with parliamentary club"
        : association.legal_status;
}
if (Q.rozwoj_party_formed) {
    for (const person of (Q.rival_person_records || [])) {
        if (
            person.organisation == "rozwoj_plus" &&
            person.party == "independent"
        ) {
            person.party = "rozwoj";
            person.loyalty = "Rozwój+";
            person.status = "Rozwój+ MP";
        }
    }
}
if (
    Q.rozwoj_party_formed &&
    Q.matysiak_party == "independent" &&
    Q.matysiak_has_sejm_mandate &&
    (Number(Q.other_seats) || 0) > 0
) {
    Q.other_seats -= 1;
    Q.rozwoj_seats = (Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) || 0) + 1;
    Q.matysiak_party = "rozwoj";
    Q.matysiak_status = "Rozwój+ MP and developmental-current organiser";
    Q.rozwoj_party_result += " · Matysiak joins from the independent benches";
    if (association) {
        association.exclusive_seats = Q.rozwoj_seats;
        association.mp_count = Math.max(
            Number(association.mp_count) || 0,
            Q.rozwoj_seats
        );
    }
}
Q.news_headline = Q.rozwoj_party_result;
!}

= October 2026 — [+ rozwoj_party_result +]

<span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span> has offices, organisers and the deputies who followed
him out of **Jarosław Kaczyński's** PiS. **Olga Semeniuk-Patkowska, Janusz
Cieszyński** and <span class="party-pis"><b>Paweł Jabłoński</b></span> can organise a parliamentary current; the
test today is whether Rozwój+ can also sustain a legal party, local lists and a
common programme.

[? if rozwoj_party_formed: The organisation registers as a political party.
Its Sejm club now has an electoral vehicle of its own, formally ending the claim
that this is merely an internal PiS current.?][? if rozwoj_club_formed and not
rozwoj_party_formed: The recognised Sejm club postpones registration. It can
negotiate and vote under one leadership, but it still lacks a party able to put
that name on ballots across Poland.?][? if not rozwoj_club_formed: Without
fifteen completed departures, Rozwój+ remains an association around an informal
parliamentary circle. Morawiecki has not yet built either a club or a party.?]
[? if matysiak_party = "rozwoj": <span class="party-razem"><b>Paulina Matysiak</b></span>, the independent deputy
associated with developmental politics, joins the new party and gives its
economic argument a bridge beyond the old PiS camp.?]

This result belongs to Rozwój+'s organisers. Lewica chooses whether to open a
limited channel, attempt an ideologically explosive merger, contest the record
or recruit local people one by one.

- @pis_party_alliance
- @pis_party_left_invite
- @pis_party_attack
- @pis_party_recruit

@pis_party_alliance
title: Offer an electoral non-aggression channel
subtitle: Define districts and issues where neither side will manufacture a common enemy; promise neither coalition nor shared lists.
on-arrival: coalition_opportunity_pis += 4; pis_relation += 1; news_headline = "Lewica tests a limited non-aggression channel"

[? if rozwoj_party_formed: Morawiecki accepts talks between two registered
parties while keeping his conservative programme intact. Both sides gain room
to fight PiS without pretending they have become one bloc.?][? if not
rozwoj_party_formed: Lewica opens a channel to Rozwój+'s organisers, but there
is no independent party with which to sign an electoral pact. The offer remains
a set of personal and parliamentary understandings.?] Kaczyński treats even
that limit as help for a defection he wants voters to punish.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the district talks

@pis_party_left_invite
title: Invite Rozwój+ into a social-development merger
subtitle: Offer Morawiecki one party of work, welfare and investment, and make every cultural and constitutional incompatibility explicit.
choose-if: rozwoj_party_formed = 1 and left_poll >= 14 and party_system_left_pull >= 18 and left_right_score >= 42 and cultural_issue_salience <= 50
unavailable-subtitle: One side still treats the cultural axis or its old bloc loyalty as decisive.
on-arrival: left_realign_invite_rozwoj = 1; rozwoj_relation += 8; coalition_opportunity_pis += 5; labor_credibility += 2; progressives_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica offers Rozwój+ a common party built around work, welfare and investment"

Lewica offers a merger congress built around industrial policy, public
investment, wages and social insurance. Morawiecki receives a route out of the
PiS inheritance; Lewica receives the possibility of governing beyond its old
electorate. The price is immediate and public: feminists, constitutionalists
and cultural progressives demand to know which conservative positions are
being imported with him. An invitation has opened negotiations, not completed
a merger.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the merger invitation

@pis_party_attack
title: Attack Rozwój+'s programme and governing record
subtitle: Make the new vehicle—or the association still trying to become one—answer for Morawiecki's premiership.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 4; public_trust += 1; pis_relation -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica denies Rozwój+ a consequence-free rebrand"

Lewica compares Rozwój+'s promises with taxes, labour policy and public-service
choices made under Morawiecki. [? if rozwoj_party_formed: The new party enters
its first campaign defending a past it hoped registration would place behind
it.?][? if not rozwoj_party_formed: The attack denies an unfinished
organisation the prestige of novelty, though it also gives Morawiecki the
national contest he needs to build one.?] PiS applauds the indictment and omits
its own signature from the same record.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the record beside the promises

@pis_party_recruit
title: Recruit individual local organisers, not the parliamentary wing
subtitle: Individual municipal organisers strengthen Lewica's local reach and future bargaining; no MP moves with them automatically.
on-arrival: local_network += 3; coalition_opportunity_pis += 2; news_headline = "Lewica recruits individuals without transferring a whole camp"

Lewica approaches municipal organisers, policy specialists and trade-union
contacts with individual offers. No Sejm mandate changes column and Morawiecki's
leadership is not delivered in a package. A few local networks become shared or
contested terrain; Rozwój+ learns that building outside PiS also means watching
its own people receive alternatives.

- @poland_event_queue: Make the individual offers

@october_judiciary_horizon
# prose-audit: Grade A — The serving Justice Minister and President enact the conflict without exposing decision scores, Lewica's authority follows its ministry rather than cabinet colour, and all six outcomes receive institutional aftermaths.
title: The judicial-status bill reaches the Palace
subtitle: Appointments, judgments and individual remedies now depend on the President
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 38
