view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority =
    Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government && Q.justice_minister_party == "Lewica" ? 1 : 0;
Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 2;
Q.judiciary_horizon_roll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 11) - 5;
if (Q.judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority) {
    const horizonHostile = Q.pres_2025_hostile_president || [
        "Andrzej Duda", String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
        "Sławomir Mentzen", "Grzegorz Braun"
    ].includes(Q.president_name);
    Q.judiciary_horizon_score = Math.round(
        44 +
        ((Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) - 35) * 0.35 +
        (Number(Q.president_judiciary_cooperation) || 0) * 0.18 +
        (horizonHostile ? -10 : 8) + Q.judiciary_horizon_roll
    );
    if (Q.judiciary_horizon_score >= 50) {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Signed";
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 1;
        Q.legal_dualism -= 4;
        Q.krs_independence += 3;
        Q.judicial_vacancies -= 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 12;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 6;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " signs the judicial-status package";
    } else if (Q.judiciary_horizon_score >= 35) {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action =
            "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal";
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
        Q.court_backlog += 2;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " refers the judicial-status package";
    } else {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Vetoed";
        Q.president_veto_count =
            (Number(Q.president_veto_count) || 0) + 1;
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
        Q.legal_dualism += 2;
        Q.court_backlog += 2;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " vetoes the judicial-status package";
    }
} else {
    Q.judiciary_horizon_score = 0;
    Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = Q.caretaker_government
        ? "No cabinet bill during caretaker government"
        : (Q.government_party == "pis"
            ? "PiS cabinet maintains the disputed system"
            : "Another cabinet controls the bill and Palace response");
    Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
    Q.news_headline = Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action;
}
!}

= October 2026 — Sign, veto or refer

The proposed status law separates appointment cohorts, preserves most
judgments, restructures disputed chambers and gives individual remedies to
people whose cases carry the institutional conflict.

[? if judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority: Justice Minister **[+
justice_minister +]**, serving from Lewica, has carried the cabinet bill to **[+
president_name +]**. The President has **[+
judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]** it. Lewica owns both the ambition of
the text and the duty not to describe a blocked bill as law.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and caretaker_government: A
caretaker cabinet has not sent a structural bill. Judges and court users remain
on case-by-case remedies until a government wins confidence.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and not caretaker_government and
left_in_government: Justice Minister **[+ justice_minister +]** is not a Lewica
minister. Status: **[+ judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]**. Lewica can
press a coalition bill and vote on it, but cannot issue instructions from a
ministry it does not hold.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and not caretaker_government and
not left_in_government: Justice Minister **[+ justice_minister +]** answers to
another cabinet. Status: **[+ judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]**.
Lewica may legislate and scrutinise from opposition; it cannot enact, withdraw
or accept a veto for somebody else's government.?]

- @horizon_judicial_bargain
- @horizon_judicial_campaign
- @horizon_judicial_delay
- @horizon_judicial_opposition
- @horizon_judicial_opposition_record
- @horizon_judicial_caretaker

@horizon_judicial_bargain
title: Implement the signed law under a published appointments protocol
subtitle: Publish the sequence, reasons and remedies so implementation cannot become another private personnel bargain.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Signed"
on-arrival: president_relation += 3; president_judiciary_cooperation += 4; progressives_dissent += 3; court_user_trust += 3; news_headline = "A signed repair law enters implementation under a published protocol"

The ministry and Palace publish appointment dates, reasons and the route for
individual challenges. Court users can see when the signed law reaches their
case; the President cannot quietly renegotiate its personnel clauses. Lewica's
radicals object that cooperation has preserved too much of the disputed system,
but implementation begins under rules they can inspect.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the appointment dates

@horizon_judicial_campaign
title: Accept the veto and campaign on the full repair mandate
subtitle: Obey the veto, name the cases it leaves unresolved and seek a new parliamentary mandate.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Vetoed"
on-arrival: president_relation -= 8; judicial_repair_mandate += 6; media_capacity += 3; legal_dualism += 3; court_backlog += 3; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 9; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 9; news_headline = "The judicial package becomes a 2027 mandate"

The cabinet does not implement a vetoed statute. Instead, Lewica places judges,
litigants and delayed cases beside the clauses **[+ president_name +]** rejected
and carries the whole package toward 2027. The constitutional line is clean;
the courts still live with vacancies, parallel authorities and another year of
delay.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the package toward 2027

@horizon_judicial_delay
title: Contest the referral while continuing individual review
subtitle: Challenge the Tribunal route without treating a referred bill as enacted law.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal"
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 5; european_judgment_compliance += 3; court_backlog += 3; public_trust -= 1; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -5; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += -4; news_headline = "The cabinet contests the referral without pretending the bill is law"

The Justice Ministry disputes the competence and composition of the Tribunal
panel, files every argument and keeps individual European-judgment remedies
open. It issues no structural change under the suspended bill. Court users gain
legal honesty and lose time while institutions contest which court may decide
the fate of a law not yet in force.

- @poland_event_queue: Dispute the panel

@horizon_judicial_opposition
title: Publish a Lewica status bill and a court-user remedy ledger
subtitle: Without the Justice Ministry, drafting and casework can expose a route but cannot alter appointments. Cost: 1 resource.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No legislative and legal team is available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; judicial_repair_mandate += 3; court_user_trust += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; media_capacity += 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 8; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += 7; news_headline = "Lewica publishes the repair it would legislate without claiming cabinet power"

Lewica publishes the full text beside a ledger of vacancies, disputed
appointments and people seeking individual remedies. [? if left_in_government:
The dossier becomes a demand from inside the coalition to Justice Minister **[+
justice_minister +]**; it does not transfer the ministry to us.?][? if not
left_in_government: From opposition, it supplies a bill the cabinet can adopt,
amend or reject and a public record of the cost of doing nothing.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Publish bill and ledger together

@horizon_judicial_opposition_record
title: Table the status bill without a staffed remedy ledger
subtitle: Preserve a parliamentary position without claiming casework, ministerial command or implementation.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 0
on-arrival: judicial_repair_mandate += 1; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "Lewica tables a basic judicial-status bill from opposition"

The club files the clauses and secures a bill number. [? if left_in_government:
Coalition partners must choose whether it receives government time, while the
non-Lewica Justice Minister retains executive authority.?][? if not
left_in_government: The opposition record fixes what Lewica would vote for but
cannot move a single appointment.?] Without a remedy team, affected court users
remain names in the argument rather than clients with help.

- @poland_event_queue: Secure the bill number

@horizon_judicial_caretaker
title: Preserve case-by-case remedies until a cabinet wins confidence
subtitle: Keep files and legal aid alive without asking a caretaker to settle the whole constitutional order.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 1
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 2; court_backlog += 2; judicial_vacancies += 1; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "The caretaker defers a structural bill while courts use individual remedies"

Lewica's lawyers and court-user groups keep individual applications moving while
the caretaker refrains from a structural settlement it cannot carry through
Parliament. Vacancies and backlog grow, but no temporary minister converts an
emergency tenure into a constitutional fait accompli. The next confidence
majority inherits both the unresolved bill and its documented human cost.

- @poland_event_queue: Keep the applications moving
